{"numberOfHits":1,"results":[{"id":"GO:0098678","isObsolete":false,"name":"viral tropism switching","definition":{"text":"A process by which the range of hosts which a virus can bind and infect is changed. Examples include phages that switch between types of fibers via the action of a virally encoded invertase.","xrefs":[{"dbCode":"PMID","dbId":"6232613"},{"dbCode":"VZ","dbId":"4498"}]},"history":[{"timestamp":"2024-09-05","action":"Added","category":"CONSTRAINT","text":"Bad taxon ID"},{"timestamp":"2022-11-22","action":"Deleted","category":"DEFINITION","text":"A process by which the range of hosts which a virus can bind and infect is changed.  Examples include phages that switch between types of fibers via the action of a virally encoded invertase."},{"timestamp":"2022-11-22","action":"Added","category":"DEFINITION","text":"A process by which the range of hosts which a virus can bind and infect is changed. Examples include phages that switch between types of fibers via the action of a virally encoded invertase."},{"timestamp":"2017-01-22","action":"Added","category":"DEFINITION","text":"A process by which the range of hosts which a virus can bind and infect is changed.  Examples include phages that switch between types of fibers via the action of a virally encoded invertase."},{"timestamp":"2017-01-22","action":"Added","category":"TERM","text":"viral tropism switching"},{"timestamp":"2017-01-22","action":"Added","category":"XREF","text":"VZ:4498"},{"timestamp":"2017-01-22","action":"Added","category":"RELATION","text":"is a GO:0016032 (viral process)"}],"xRefs":[{"dbCode":"UniProtKB-KW","dbId":"KW-1264","name":"Viral receptor tropism switching"},{"dbCode":"VZ","dbId":"4498"}],"taxonConstraints":[{"ancestorId":"GO:0098678","ancestorName":"viral tropism switching","relationship":"never_in_taxon","taxId":"4896","taxIdType":"NCBITaxon","taxName":"Schizosaccharomyces pombe"}],"aspect":"biological_process","usage":"Unrestricted","goDiscussions":[{"title":"Viral Processes